  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_030",
  "text": "Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 13 Henson Park\n\nClause 9.13.1 - heritage (heritage): The precinct contains two Heritage Conservation Areas being the Audley Street South (Bayswater Estate) Heritage Conservation Area and the majority of the Norwood Park Estate Heritage Conservation Area.\n\nClause 9.13.1 - setback (development_control): Front setbacks are generally consistent within each street with a setback of 2 metres to 4 metres the most common.\n\nClause 9.13.1 - parking (development_control): In areas of the precinct where off street parking is provided, it is most frequently at the rear of the property accessed by a rear lane or via a side driveway.\n\nClause 9.13.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and encourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.\n\nClause 9.13.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect the identified Heritage Items within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.13.2 - height_limit (development_control): To maintain distinctly single storey streetscapes that exist within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.13.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect groups or runs of buildings which retain their original built form including roof forms, original detailing and finishes.\n\nClause 9.13.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect significant streetscapes and/or public domain elements within the precinct including landscaping, fencing, open space, sandstone kerbing and guttering, views and vistas and prevailing subdivision patterns.\n\n",
  "metadata": {
    "document_name": "Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 13 Henson Park",
    "extractions_count": 13
  }
